    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d259">

                <pb facs="0367" n="247" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg247"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Chargé Snyder.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-08-11"><hi rendition="#italic">August 11,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 31.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 62 of July 4 last, reporting the murder of an American citizen, Joseff Otto,
                    in the Department of Antioquia.</p>
                <p>In reply I have to say that the Department is gratified to see that the Colombian
                    Government is taking appropriate measures to secure the apprehension of the
                    perpetrators.</p>
                <p>The report of the circumstances of the case is awaited by the Department.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. B. Loomis.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
